    "SYNTHETIC CORPUS. Padding vectors are Gaussian perturbations of real embeddings, renormalized to the same unit length, targeting cosine 0.85 to their parent. They carry NO semantic content, so every quality field is null and assertNoSemanticClaim refuses a record that fills one in. The only claims here are about the index and the query plan.",
    "ann_recall_vs_exact is an INDEX property: overlap between the HNSW result and the SAME query run with index scans disabled. Ground truth is derived by this harness, so no provider is involved and the whole experiment is credential-independent.",
    "Domain shape is held at production selectivity (~8.5 skills per domain) at EVERY corpus size, because production grows by adding domains, not by enlarging them. Letting domains grow instead would make the filter less selective as the table grows and would hide the filtered-ANN shortfall this experiment exists to find.",
    "Zero provider calls. Zero writes outside the taxonomy_scale_sim schema."
